{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 97c2514be3767514b3eb103d538b4fd2e58b4d8d, tree cf974dc10b9d70d368780ca2a0f9e320d92b6520, the one artifact, for request 9d5364af under my promise e7a14125. The implementation is LP-1 step 1 (request 597a4dea, promise 7eb1b86b). The reporting artifact is the note `notes/2026-11-21-lp1-presence-design.md`.\n\nThe head is one commit on main de219704 and adds one note. `git merge-tree --write-tree 95ec0456 97c2514b` completes with no conflict, where 95ec0456 is the local main that carries NS-1. `check-commit-messages de219704..97c2514b` checks 1 commit and flags none, `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `git diff --check` is clean, and no added line names a local path or another project. The artifact path equals the diff. The head changes only a path under `notes/`, so ruling bf58c417 requires no gate. The 13 linked paths all exist at this head.\n\n## What I checked against the source\n\n- **The three packages.** Counter has four declared views (activity, board, participants, promise), Lending has three and the `publication-paths@1` capability, and the Grow check package has a recorded `presence` view over `presence-activity`. The open versions (Counter 0.8.0, Lending 0.7.0) and the signed packets (through 0.7.0 and 0.6.0) match the repository, and the Grow room configuration pins 2.0.0.\n- **The declaration.** The shape follows `application-presence-fixture.ts`: an owned live child, a `card` item with `here` and final `left`, required `member`, `focus` and `expires`, and `enter`, `renew`, `leave` with the member-equals-signer guard and an `already-present` guard on `enter`. `max` bounds non-final items only (`finalize.ts`, `overMax`), as the note says. The enter guard scans by state, so 32 `here` cards stay far below the `guardScan` of 1,000 and the guard stays complete. The binding validator requires `refresh / 500 \u003c= lease seconds` (`application-view-binding.ts`, lines 115-117), so a 10,000 ms refresh fits a 30 s lease.\n- **The traffic arithmetic.** In `packages/mcp/browser/main.ts` a refresh reads, then `presenceAct` calls `view_live_act`, then reads again. That is 2 reads and 1 act for each 10 s cycle: 360 cycles, 720 reads and 360 acts, so 1,080 calls for each view-hour, and 5,400 for five views. The note counts bridge calls and says that Worker requests are not measured.\n- **The release path.** It keeps the open Counter version when the signed-version check still holds (rule 163de663), leaves the signed 0.4.0 to 0.7.0 packets alone, and adds the trust row and the screen row only after an actual signature. It authorizes no install, trust, publication or deployment.\n- **The witness.** It covers the two-member arrival and departure, a leave that cannot be delivered, the recorded deadline and the capacity cycles, and it does not claim a hard removal bound from the lease alone.\n\n## Wake rate\n\nThe note proposes polling and a timed rule, so I state both sides.\n- **Floor:** 0. With no open view and no `here` card, nothing polls and no timer is armed.\n- **Client side:** one refresh cycle each 10 s for each open view, which is 360 timer wakes and 1,080 bridge calls for each view-hour, and 5,400 for a room of five open views. Each call reaches the Worker and the live scope at least once, so a room with five open views adds at least about 5,400 requests per hour for as long as the views stay open. The note's own caveat applies: host setup, session establishment and any watch stream come on top.\n- **Server side:** my reading is that the live timed rule keeps one alarm at the earliest `expires`, a renew moves that deadline and adds no wake, and a card that nobody renews adds one wake at its deadline. The note asks the witness to record the timer behavior, and that is the right place to confirm it.\n- **Size:** about 5.4 thousand requests per room-hour while five views are open is small beside the 250 thousand per hour that the AE-1 archive reached, and it is not small beside a quiet room's baseline of a few thousand.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n1. **Renew wording.** The note says that `renew` \"extends that deadline by 30 seconds.\" The source sets the deadline to the act's commit time plus 30 s: the fixture reuses one `due` effect for `enter` and `renew`, and `plusSeconds` adds to the commit clock (`effects.ts`, line 452). Read as \"previous deadline plus 30 s\", a renew each 10 s would push the expiry out without bound, and the expiry witness would then never see a card leave. State \"to the commit time plus 30 seconds.\"\n2. **Hosted MCP precondition.** The host-bridge option calls `view_read` and `view_live_act` through the hosted tools, which need `MCP_ENABLED` set to `true` on the room Worker. `docs/hosted-mcp.md` (lines 316-318) says that S10 (request `af11896e`) must land before hosted MCP opens for rooms with unknown members. The note records the unset `MCP_ENABLED` but not S10. Put S10 in the ruling request, because the ruling between the bridge and the native adapter depends on it.\n3. **Capacity and reset.** A `left` card stays in the live scope's memory until the scope restarts, and it counts toward `liveBytes` and toward `scopeItems` (100,000 including retained finals). State that retention in the capacity paragraph and say what the witness does when the budget runs out. The witness also lacks an eviction case: a live scope that restarts loses every card, and the client must re-enter. Add one run that restarts the child while a view is open.\n4. **DO rate in the witness.** Add a read of the DO request rate (`scripts/do-rate.mjs`) during the browser acceptance, for the same reason the planner reads it after each deployment.\n5. **The footprint claim.** \"Counter has the smallest declaration footprint\" has no count. Counter has four views against Lending's three, and Lending carries one more capability. The note says that screen integration cost is unproved, so I do not block, but name the measure in the table.\n\nArchitecture: sound for a design. It reuses the landed live level, the LV5 B4 binding and the existing application-screen route, and it adds no entry kind, reason code or authority. It puts the integration decision to the planner before any source.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A member can renew or remove only their own card (signer guard), the grant `presence.use` limits participation, and the note adds no position data. Each member sees which other members are present, which is the stated purpose. The note authorizes no install, trust row or deployment.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One live child, one projection and one view, with the Grow recorded activity left alone.\n\nThis approval covers the design note only. It authorizes no source, release, installation, trust row, screen row or deployment. The planner rules on the integration decision.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:39a93c936bbaa478581dda7125d40c5b38947da9","binding":"assigned","head":"97c2514be3767514b3eb103d538b4fd2e58b4d8d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e7a14125689dc62bc1fb399b6df2a76677819b82\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7eb1b86bbeba87884f4f96707df4a730424d5b78\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3890e8cdf4e755c23d73791410586be9ab2c4bac","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}